    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for virtio-win.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 9.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "The virtio-win package provides paravirtualized network drivers for most\nMicrosoft Windows operating systems. Paravirtualized drivers are\nvirtualization-aware drivers used by fully virtualized guests running on Rocky Enterprise Software Foundation\nEnterprise Linux. Fully virtualized guests using the paravirtualized drivers\ngain significantly better I/O performance than fully virtualized guests running\nwithout the drivers.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
